============================================================
TMA B-TILE EXPERIMENT — SUMMARY
============================================================
Date:           2026-08-13
Platform:       win32, sm_120 (RTX 5060), CUDA 13.3, nvcc 13.3 / VS2026
Variant source: kernels/src/register_tiled_gemm_TMA_B.cu
Accepted source: kernels/src/register_tiled_gemm.cu (UNCHANGED)

VERDICT: REJECT / NOISE — B-only TMA does NOT, under the established
        gate, improve the accepted kernel (+/- 1% inconsistent band).

============================================================
TMA TOOLCHAIN PROOF: PASS
============================================================
API used:
  - Host tensormap encode: cuda::__driver::__tensorMapEncodeTiled
    (resolves cuTensorMapEncodeTiled proc at runtime; no dlpack dep).
    Rank 3, FLOAT32:
      globalDim    = { N(cols,fastest), K(rows), 1 }
      globalStrides= { N*4 bytes row stride, N*4*K bytes outer } (bytes)
      boxDim       = { 64, 16, 1 }
      elementStrides = {1,1,1}
    IMPORTANT: cuTensorMap is COLUMN-major (dim[0] = fastest/contiguous),
    and tensorRank MUST be 3/4/5 (2 is INVALID). Strides are in BYTES.
  - Device copy:    cuda::ptx::cp_async_bulk_tensor (space_shared,space_global,
                    &Bs[0][0], tm_dev_ptr, coords{col_start,k_base,0}, &mbar)
  - Sync:           cuda::ptx::mbarrier_init / mbarrier_arrive / 
                    mbarrier_arrive_expect_tx / mbarrier_try_wait_parity,
                    arrival count = 256, expected tx bytes = 4096/tile.
  - Tensormap MUST live in DEVICE GLOBAL memory (kernel must receive a
    CUtensorMap* pointer). Passing the by-value 128-byte CUtensorMap kernel
    parameter to TMA caused illegal-access (param/const-space map not usable).

Instruction evidence (final SASS, register_tiled_gemm_TMA_B_sass.log):
  UTMALDG.3D [URdst], [URmap];      (Blackwell Unified TMA load-to-shared, .3D)
  mbarrier.arrive.expect_tx.release.cta.shared::cta.b64
  mbarrier.try_wait.parity.shared::cta.b64
  PTX: cp.async.bulk.tensor.3d.shared::cta.global.tile.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes
Small proof (tma_proof.cu): a single 16x64 tile copied via TMA to shared and
  read back: 0 mismatches, maxerr 0.000000  => PASS.

